# Normalise line endings in the repository so a Windows checkout does not
# rewrite every file, and so the build inputs stay byte-stable.
#
# The BOM rule matters more than it looks: app.py used to carry a UTF-8 BOM
# (EF BB BF). Python imports it fine, but `ast.parse()` — which
# streamlit-desktop-app runs while building the .exe — rejects it with
# "invalid non-printable character U+FEFF". That is an invisible bug until the
# desktop build fails. `working-tree-encoding` is deliberately NOT set to
# anything: it would have git rewrite files in place, which is exactly what
# caused the problem in the first place.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.py text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.txt text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
